From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0261: fingerprint unlock (kernel side)

The touch driver reports when a finger is on the fingerprint spot
(kern.sweet_fod_press, 1 while a touch is inside the circle at 540,2109
r 105 panel pixels; kern.sweet_fod_seq counts presses). kern.sweet_qsee op 26
lights the spot and authenticates again and again until a match, the finger
off the spot for over 150 ms, or 3 s, then turns the spot off; a match is
kept with its time, failures count up to 5, after which op 26 asks for the
passcode until the next good one. Op 27 asks AppleKeyStore
(sweet_aks_biometric_unlock) to unlock with a match under 3 s old: only with a
passcode set, the device unlocked with it since boot and locked now; it then
does what a good passcode does (unlocked, failures cleared, the same
interest messages). Ops 26 and 27 log one summary line per attempt.
---
